# SABOTAGE: A4 (ADR-047 §5.3 / RP-AG-5) gate sabotage — the APPROVAL-STATE GUARD is
# dropped: `verify_approval/4` stops re-loading the approval row and simply TRUSTS the
# struct it was handed. `execute_approved/3` is public (the E3 handler lives in its own
# module), and the only field an attacker needs is the approval id — which is not a secret:
# it sits verbatim in the token-only `atn_meta.approval_id` jsonb of the turn row, in the
# clear, right next to the proposal. With the guard gone, a bare `%{id: <real id>}` map, a
# still-PENDING approval, or an APPROVED approval belonging to ANOTHER ORG each executes
# the parked write — with no `pending -> approved` transition, no distinct-party decision,
# and NO `approval_approved` audit event. The human approval becomes decorative. The three
# named reds must flip; the real-engine positive control stays green, proving what was lost
# is the verification and not the execution path.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_write_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a still-PENDING approval cannot execute the parked write at the seam
# MUST_FAIL: a FORGED bare-map approval refuses
# MUST_FAIL: an APPROVED approval belonging to ANOTHER org
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex
